================================================================================
1. OVERVIEW & TECHNICAL STACK
================================================================================

Restaurant Manager is a full-featured Point-of-Sale (POS) desktop application
built for restaurant and food-service businesses. It manages orders, inventory,
payments, receipts, analytics/reports, user roles, and branding — all from a
single modern Windows application.

TECHNOLOGY STACK:
  • Framework:        WPF (.NET 8.0), C#
  • UI Toolkit:       WPF-UI 4.2.0 (FluentWindow, Mica backdrop)
  • Database:         SQLite via Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite 8.0.0
  • MVVM Toolkit:     CommunityToolkit.Mvvm 8.2.1
  • JSON:             Newtonsoft.Json 13.0.3
  • HTTP:             Microsoft.Extensions.Http 8.0.0
  • Target:           net8.0-windows, Nullable enabled, Latest C# language
  • Architecture:     Code-behind pattern with static service instances on App
  • DB Location:      %AppData%/RestaurantManager/restaurant.db

================================================================================
2. AUTHENTICATION & USER MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

LOGIN SYSTEM:
  • Email + Password authentication
  • Role-based access control with three roles:
      – Developer: Full access to all features and settings
      – Admin:     Access to orders, inventory, reports, and limited settings
      – Staff:     Access to orders and dashboard only
  • Demo login accounts (toggleable via Developer settings)
  • Close confirmation dialog on login window exit

USER ROLES & PERMISSIONS:
  ┌──────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Role         │ Access                                                │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Developer    │ All features, all admin settings tabs, Developer tab, │
  │              │ can assign Developer role to users                    │
  │ Admin        │ Dashboard, Orders, Inventory, Reports, limited        │
  │              │ settings (Login Form, Users, Departments, Categories) │
  │ Staff        │ Dashboard, Orders only                                │
  └──────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

USER PROPERTIES:
  • Name, Email, Password
  • Role (comma-separated: developer, admin, staff)
  • Department (kitchen, service, bar, housekeeping, front-desk, cashier)
  • Status (active / inactive)
  • CreatedAt, UpdatedAt timestamps

================================================================================
3. DASHBOARD
================================================================================

The Dashboard is the main landing page after login. It provides an at-a-glance
overview of business performance with four customizable summary cards.

SUMMARY CARDS (4):
  • Total Revenue       – Sum of all completed order totals
  • Today's Orders      – Count of orders placed today
  • Menu Items          – Total number of active menu/inventory items
  • Low Stock Alerts    – Count of items below their minimum stock level

FEATURES:
  • Dynamic currency formatting (default: ₦ Naira)
  • Card background gradients are customizable via Admin Settings (Theme Colors)
  • Card text color is configurable
  • Real-time data refresh on view load
  • Quick action buttons for common tasks
  • Recent orders list with status indicators

================================================================================
4. ORDERS MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

The Orders module is the core POS functionality, supporting multi-tab ordering,
full payment processing, receipt generation, and order history management.

─── 4.1 MULTI-TAB ORDER SYSTEM ───

  • Create multiple simultaneous orders via tabs
  • Each tab represents an independent order with its own cart
  • "+" button to add new order tabs
  • Tab header shows order number
  • Switch between tabs without losing data
  • Close individual tabs (with confirmation if items exist)
  • Each tab maintains its own state (items, notes, table number)

─── 4.2 MENU & ITEM SELECTION ───

  • Grid display of available inventory items
  • Search bar to filter items by name
  • Category-based filtering
  • Each item card shows:
      – Item name and category
      – Price (formatted with dynamic currency)
      – Available stock quantity
  • Click to add item to current order tab
  • Quantity adjustment (increment/decrement) in cart
  • Remove individual items from cart
  • Real-time total calculation

─── 4.3 ORDER CART ───

  • Right-side panel showing current order items
  • Per-item: name, quantity, unit price, line total
  • Quantity controls (+/-) for each item
  • Delete button to remove items
  • Order notes field
  • Running subtotal and total display
  • Clear cart option
  • "Back" button with unsaved changes warning

─── 4.4 PAYMENT SYSTEM ───

  Full-screen payment overlay with four payment methods:

  • 💵 Cash Payment:
      – Enter amount tendered
      – Automatic change calculation
      – Quick-amount buttons
      – Validates sufficient payment

  • 💳 Card Payment:
      – Reference number input
      – Direct completion

  • 🏦 Bank Transfer:
      – Reference number input
      – Direct completion

  • 📱 Mobile Payment:
      – Reference number input
      – Direct completion

  Payment flow:
    1. Click "Complete Order" or "Pay" button
    2. Payment overlay appears (full-screen)
    3. Select payment method
    4. Enter required details
    5. Confirm payment
    6. Order status changes to "completed"
    7. PaymentMethod recorded on order
    8. Receipt auto-generated
    9. Inventory quantities automatically decremented

─── 4.5 ORDER HISTORY ───

  • View all past orders in scrollable list
  • Each order card displays:
      – Selection checkbox (for bulk operations)
      – Status icon (emoji-coded)
      – Order number, date/time, item count
      – Total amount (formatted currency)
      – Action buttons (View, Edit, Delete)
  • Search orders by order number
  • Filter by status: All, Pending, Preparing, Completed, Cancelled
  • View order details with full item breakdown

  Edit capabilities (for non-completed orders):
    – Modify quantities
    – Remove items
    – Add notes
    – Change status

  Actions on completed orders:
    – View details
    – Print receipt
    – Process payment (if unpaid)

─── 4.6 MULTI-SELECT & BULK DELETE ───

  • Checkbox on each order card for selection
  • "Select All" checkbox in filter bar
  • "Delete Selected (N)" button showing count
  • Bulk delete with confirmation dialog
  • Selection state tracked via HashSet

─── 4.7 ORDER STATUSES ───

  ┌────────────┬────────┬───────────────────────────┐
  │ Status     │ Icon   │ Description               │
  ├────────────┼────────┼───────────────────────────┤
  │ Pending    │ 🟡     │ Order placed, not started  │
  │ Preparing  │ 🔵     │ Being prepared             │
  │ Completed  │ 🟢     │ Fulfilled and paid         │
  │ Cancelled  │ 🔴     │ Order was cancelled        │
  └────────────┴────────┴───────────────────────────┘

================================================================================
5. INVENTORY MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

Full inventory tracking system with stock levels, categories, cost tracking,
and low-stock alerts.

─── 5.1 INVENTORY ITEMS ───

  Each item tracks:
    • Name                    – Item name
    • Description             – Optional description
    • Category                – Assigned category (e.g., Proteins, Produce)
    • Quantity                – Current stock count
    • Unit                    – Unit of measurement (e.g., kg, pcs, liters)
    • Cost Price              – Cost per unit (for stock valuation)
    • Minimum Level           – Threshold for low-stock alerts
    • Reorder Quantity        – Suggested reorder amount
    • Stock Value             – Computed: Quantity × CostPrice
    • CreatedAt / UpdatedAt   – Timestamps

─── 5.2 INVENTORY MANAGEMENT FEATURES ───

  • View all items in scrollable list/grid
  • Search items by name
  • Filter by category
  • Add new items with full details
  • Edit existing items
  • Delete items (with confirmation)
  • Stock level indicators (color-coded):
      – Green: Stock above minimum level
      – Yellow: Stock at or near minimum level
      – Red: Stock below minimum level (low stock alert)
  • Inventory adjustments log (InventoryLog entity)
  • Automatic stock deduction when orders are completed

─── 5.3 CATEGORIES ───

  Categories organize inventory items:
    • Name (e.g., Proteins, Produce, Dry Goods)
    • Icon (emoji, e.g., 🥩, 🥬, 🌾)
    • Color (hex color code)
    • Association with Departments via CategoryDepartment join table
    • Managed in Admin Settings → Categories tab

─── 5.4 DEPARTMENTS ───

  Departments organize business operations:
    • Name (e.g., Eatery/Restaurant, Lounge, Shawarma Spot)
    • Icon (emoji, e.g., 🍽, 🛋, 🌯)
    • Color (hex color code)
    • User assignment via UserDepartment join table
    • Category assignment via CategoryDepartment join table
    • Managed in Admin Settings → Departments tab

================================================================================
6. REPORTS & ANALYTICS
================================================================================

Comprehensive reporting dashboard with 9 analytical sections, date filtering,
and CSV export capability. Accessible to Admin and Developer roles only.

─── 6.1 DATE FILTERS ───

  • Today          – Current day only
  • This Week      – Current week
  • This Month     – Current month (default)
  • This Year      – Current year
  • Custom Range   – User-defined start and end dates

─── 6.2 REPORT SECTIONS ───

  1. SUMMARY CARDS
     • Total Revenue (formatted with currency)
     • Total Orders count
     • Average Order Value
     • Total Items Sold
     • Period-over-period comparison

  2. REVENUE CHART
     • Bar chart drawn on Canvas
     • Revenue plotted by date
     • Visual revenue trends over selected period

  3. PAYMENT METHOD BREAKDOWN
     • Distribution across payment methods:
       – Cash, Card, Bank Transfer, Mobile
     • Progress bars showing proportion
     • Amount and percentage for each method

  4. TOP SELLING ITEMS
     • Top 10 items ranked by revenue
     • Shows item name, quantity sold, total revenue

  5. ORDER STATUS DISTRIBUTION
     • Completed, Pending, Preparing, Cancelled counts
     • Visual breakdown of order outcomes

  6. SALES BY CATEGORY
     • Revenue grouped by inventory item category
     • Category name and total revenue

  7. PEAK HOURS ANALYSIS
     • Top 8 busiest hours of the day
     • Order count per hour
     • Helps with staffing decisions

  8. STAFF PERFORMANCE
     • Per-user order count and revenue
     • Staff member name, orders handled, total revenue

  9. DAILY BREAKDOWN TABLE
     • Tabular format showing last 14 days
     • Columns: Date, Orders, Completed, Revenue

─── 6.3 CSV EXPORT ───

  • Export filtered order data to CSV file
  • Save file dialog for location selection
  • Includes order details, items, totals, dates

================================================================================
7. ADMIN SETTINGS
================================================================================

Comprehensive settings panel with 9 tabs. Tab visibility is role-restricted.

  Developer-only tabs: Branding, Currency, Theme Colors, Receipt, Developer
  Admin + Developer tabs: Login Form, Users, Departments, Categories

─── 7.1 BRANDING TAB (Developer only) ───

  • Logo Emoji:          Emoji displayed as logo fallback
  • Logo Image:          Upload company logo image (PNG/JPG)
                         – Used on receipts, login page, and as app window icon
                         – Remove option to revert to default
  • Business Name:       Line 1 and Line 2
  • Tagline:             Company tagline
  • Description:         Business description
  • Copyright Text:      Shown on login page
  • Window Title:        Application window title
  • Welcome Title:       Login page welcome heading
  • Welcome Subtitle:    Login page welcome subheading

  Live preview: Logo changes immediately update the app window icon on all
  open windows via App.ApplyLogoIcon().

─── 7.2 LOGIN FORM TAB ───

  Configure the login page appearance:
  • Welcome title and subtitle text
  • Logo display settings
  • Business name display
  • Description and tagline visibility

─── 7.3 CURRENCY TAB (Developer only) ───

  • Currency Symbol:       Default ₦ (Naira)
  • Currency Code:         Default NGN
  • Currency Position:     Before or After the amount
  • Thousands Separator:   Default comma (,)
  • Decimal Separator:     Default period (.)
  • Decimal Places:        Default 2

  All currency formatting throughout the app uses BrandingSettings.FormatCurrency()
  which respects these settings dynamically.

─── 7.4 THEME COLORS TAB (Developer only) ───

  Customize dashboard card gradients:
  • Card 1 – Gradient Color 1 & Color 2 (Total Revenue card)
  • Card 2 – Gradient Color 1 & Color 2 (Today's Orders card)
  • Card 3 – Gradient Color 1 & Color 2 (Menu Items card)
  • Card 4 – Gradient Color 1 & Color 2 (Low Stock card)
  • Card Text Color (applies to all cards)

  Color inputs accept hex color codes (e.g., #667eea).
  Changes apply immediately to the Dashboard on next load.

─── 7.5 RECEIPT TAB (Developer only) ───

  Configure printed/previewed receipt content:
  • Receipt Header:    Custom text printed at top of receipt
  • Receipt Footer:    Custom text printed at bottom of receipt
  • Header/footer appear on all generated receipts
  • Default receipt width: 42 characters (POS standard)

─── 7.6 USERS TAB ───

  Full user CRUD management:
  • View all users in a list
  • Add new user: Name, Email, Password, Role, Department, Status
  • Edit existing users
  • Delete users (with confirmation)
  • Role assignment:
      – Staff, Admin checkboxes always visible
      – Developer checkbox visible ONLY to Developer users
  • Department assignment dropdown
  • Status toggle (active/inactive)

─── 7.7 DEPARTMENTS TAB ───

  Manage business departments:
  • View all departments
  • Add new: Name, Icon (emoji), Color (hex)
  • Edit existing departments
  • Delete departments (with confirmation)

─── 7.8 CATEGORIES TAB ───

  Manage inventory categories:
  • View all categories
  • Add new: Name, Icon (emoji), Color (hex)
  • Edit existing categories
  • Delete categories (with confirmation)

─── 7.9 DEVELOPER TAB (Developer only) ───

  Developer-specific controls:
  • Show Demo Login Toggle:
      – Checkbox to show/hide demo account section on login page
      – When enabled, demo accounts with quick-login buttons appear
      – Setting persists in database (BrandingSettings.ShowDemoLogin)
  • Trademark Text:
      – Configurable text displayed in app footer areas
      – Default: "Powered by Restaurant Manager"
      – Appears in: Main window footer, sidebar bottom, login page (both panels)
      – Setting persists in database (BrandingSettings.TrademarkText)

