9. DATABASE & DATA PERSISTENCE
================================================================================

─── 9.1 DATABASE CONFIGURATION ───

  • Engine:    SQLite
  • ORM:      Entity Framework Core 8.0
  • Location: %AppData%/RestaurantManager/restaurant.db
  • Context:  RestaurantDbContext
  • Init:     EnsureCreated() + raw SQL migrations

─── 9.2 TABLES / ENTITIES ───

  ┌─────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Table               │ Purpose                                      │
  ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Users               │ User accounts with roles and departments     │
  │ Orders              │ Order header (number, status, total, payment)│
  │ OrderItems          │ Line items with quantity, price, item ref    │
  │ MenuItems           │ Menu items (legacy, for seeding)             │
  │ InventoryItems      │ Stock items with cost, quantity, levels      │
  │ InventoryLogs       │ Stock adjustment history                     │
  │ Categories          │ Item categories with icon and color          │
  │ Departments         │ Business departments with icon and color     │
  │ UserDepartments     │ User ↔ Department join table                 │
  │ CategoryDepartments │ Category ↔ Department join table             │
  │ BrandingSettings    │ All app configuration and branding           │
  │ SyncLogs            │ Change tracking for future sync              │
  └─────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘

─── 9.3 RELATIONSHIPS ───

  • Order → OrderItems:         One-to-Many (cascade delete)
  • OrderItem → InventoryItem:  Many-to-One (FK: InventoryItemId)
  • User ↔ Department:          Many-to-Many (via UserDepartments)
  • Category ↔ Department:      Many-to-Many (via CategoryDepartments)

─── 9.4 MIGRATIONS ───

  Database migrations run automatically on startup via raw SQL:
  • CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS for Categories, Departments, join tables
  • ALTER TABLE Orders ADD COLUMN PaymentMethod (with backfill of NULL → "N/A")
  • ALTER TABLE BrandingSettings ADD COLUMN ReceiptHeader
  • ALTER TABLE BrandingSettings ADD COLUMN ReceiptFooter
  • ALTER TABLE BrandingSettings ADD COLUMN ShowDemoLogin
  • ALTER TABLE BrandingSettings ADD COLUMN TrademarkText

─── 9.5 SYNC SYSTEM ───

  • SyncLog table tracks all entity changes
  • Records: EntityType, EntityId, Action (create/update/delete), JSON Data
  • IsSynced flag for future cloud synchronization
  • Currently operates in local-only mode
  • "System Online" status indicator in sidebar

================================================================================
10. CORE SERVICES & ARCHITECTURE
================================================================================

─── 10.1 SERVICE PATTERN ───

  All services are instantiated as static properties on the App class:
    • App.OrderService        – Order CRUD, item management
    • App.InventoryService    – Inventory CRUD, stock adjustments
    • App.BrandingService     – Branding settings get/save
    • App.UserService         – User authentication, CRUD
    • App.CategoryService     – Category CRUD
    • App.DepartmentService   – Department CRUD

  Services are available globally via App.ServiceName throughout the
  application without dependency injection containers.

─── 10.2 APP STARTUP SEQUENCE ───

  1. Create database directory if not exists
  2. Initialize RestaurantDbContext
  3. EnsureCreated() — create tables
  4. Run SQL migrations (ALTER TABLE statements)
  5. Seed demo data (users, menu items, inventory, categories, departments)
  6. Create all service instances
  7. Show LoginWindow

─── 10.3 KEY SERVICE METHODS ───

  OrderService:
    • GetAllOrdersAsync()         – With ThenInclude for Items → InventoryItem
    • GetOrderByIdAsync(id)       – Single order with includes
    • CreateOrderAsync(order)     – Create + SyncLog
    • UpdateOrderAsync(order)     – Update + SyncLog
    • DeleteOrderAsync(id)        – Delete + SyncLog

  InventoryService:
    • GetAllItemsAsync()          – All inventory items
    • GetItemByIdAsync(id)        – Single item
    • CreateItemAsync(item)       – Create
    • UpdateItemAsync(item)       – Update
    • DeleteItemAsync(id)         – Delete
    • AdjustStockAsync(id, qty)   – Stock adjustment with log

  BrandingService:
    • GetSettingsAsync()          – Load branding settings
    • SaveSettingsAsync(settings) – Save all branding fields

  UserService:
    • AuthenticateAsync(email, password) – Login validation
    • GetAllUsersAsync()                 – All users
    • CreateUserAsync(user)              – Create
    • UpdateUserAsync(user)              – Update
    • DeleteUserAsync(id)                – Delete

─── 10.4 ERROR HANDLING ───

  • Global exception handler catches unhandled exceptions
  • Error dialog shown to user
  • Error logged to temp file: RestaurantManager_Error.log
  • Inner exception details captured for debugging
  • Local try-catch blocks in service calls with user-friendly messages
  • Status messages displayed in UI for success/failure feedback

─── 10.5 APP ICON SYSTEM ───

  • Default app icon: app.ico (restaurant plate with fork & knife)
  • Dynamic icon: If company logo is uploaded in Branding settings,
    the logo is used as the window icon for all windows
  • App.ApplyLogoIcon(Window) helper method:
      – Checks BrandingSettings.LogoImagePath
      – Loads image as BitmapImage
      – Sets as window Icon property
      – Falls back to default app.ico if no logo or file not found

